'''Tainted Lazarus''' is a [[Characters|character]] added in [[The Binding of Isaac: Repentance]]. He is the alternate version of {{C|Lazarus}}, playable in two different states: Tainted Lazarus and Dead Tainted Lazarus. Tainted Lazarus has ragged hair and is covered in dirt while Dead Tainted Lazarus has pale white skin, glassy eyes, and is covered in blood. Horizontal scars are noticeable on the wrists of both forms of Tainted Lazarus. Tainted Lazarus is unlocked by reaching {{s|Home}} and using the {{I|Red Key}}, {{P|Cracked Key}}, or {{P|1=Soul of Cain}} to access a special room in one of the walls while playing as Lazarus.

Tainted Lazarus starts with 3 {{e|Red Heart}}s, whereas Dead Tainted Lazarus starts with 2 {{e|Soul Heart}}s. Tainted Lazarus begins with fairly low [[range]] while Dead Tainted Lazarus has a 1.5× [[damage]] multiplier, slightly lower [[tears]] and [[speed]], and −2 [[luck]]. Each character has separate items, attributes, trinkets, and consumables, similar to {{C|Jacob and Esau}}, except each character is only played individually. Whenever a room is cleared, including each wave of multi-wave rooms like in [[Greed Mode]] and {{R|Challenge Room}}s, Tainted Lazarus swaps between the two forms, essentially requiring the player to play each character on every other room. Tainted Lazarus starts with {{i|Flip}} in his consumable slot, which can be used to swap states immediately.

== Notes ==
* {{dlc|r+}} Unlike other characters, Tainted Lazarus' {{I|Flip}} only requires 4 charges.
* Correctly managing the charges of {{I|Flip}} to get items for both forms of Tainted Lazarus from {{R|Treasure Room}}s, {{R|Shop}}s, {{R|Devil Room}}s, and {{R|Angel Room}}s is very important, as grabbing every flipped item effectively doubles the power of Tainted Lazarus.
* The only way to access the ghostly form of an item generated by {{I|Flip}} is by using it to switch forms. Re-entering the room with a different form of Tainted Lazarus does not flip the item pedestals. Making Tainted Lazarus switch form inside the room without using {{I|Flip}} (for example, after fighting an angel in the Angel room), does not flip the item pedestals.
* Flipping between forms will effectively act as a room transition for certain items; in other words, flipping back in the same room will reset those items as if a new room had been entered.
* Items that grant extra lives ({{I|Dead Cat}}, {{I|1up!}}, {{I|Lazarus' Rags}}, etc.) only affect the one who picks them up. If Dead Lazarus collects an extra life item, it can only activate when Dead Lazarus is the active character, and vice versa.
* When transforming into a different character (e.g. with {{i|Clicker}}), only the current form's items will be given to the new character.
* If one form of Tainted Lazarus is reduced to zero hearts while being in the transitioning phase of Flip, he will remain alive as the other form, but die as soon as he switches back. There is nothing the other form can do to prevent that death, unless you're playing co-op and being revived after a boss death; in greedier/greed mode you will be revived if another player kills the first boss wave fought, while in XL floors, it is the 2nd boss killed that allows for a player revival while you are in the T Lazarus form that is in a baby ghost familiar form, so it's recommended to plan rooms accordingly.
* Quest items are counted as both characters having them.
** {{I|The Polaroid}} and {{I|The Negative}} work on both Living Tainted Lazarus and Dead Tainted Lazarus, regardless of which picked them up.
** {{i|Key Piece 1}} and {{i|Key Piece 2}} will grant their Angel Room bonus to both characters, and will combine to a whole key even if the pieces are not on the same character.
** {{i|Knife Piece 1}} and {{i|Knife Piece 2}} will combine to a whole knife usable by both characters regardless of who has which piece.
** {{i|Dogma}}'s flight and stat bonuses are applied to both characters, but healing and Holy Mantle apply only to the active character when receiving it. Since forms change after defeating Dogma, and the item is bestowed after the cutscene, this means that the form that was ''not'' active to defeat Dogma will receive the healing and mantle effect.
* Temporary buffs such as {{I|Razor Blade}} disappear when you switch from one character to the other. This is especially noticeable in Greed Mode.
** However, room buffs like [[I'm Drowsy]], {{p|Era Walk}}, and {{p|XI - Strength?}} will stay in effect between flips. Any stat bonuses given are lost.
* Only the character that picks up an activated item first gets the progress for related [[transformations]], so the player needs to be aware of what character needs the transformation progress.
* Tainted Lazarus takes a lot of micromanagement compared to most other characters. It can be difficult to accomplish simple tasks due to the forced switching between forms and {{I|Flip}}'s long charge time. Try to stay ahead of this, and pay close attention to what form is active and when they will shift. Something such as collecting an item from a Treasure Room or Curse Room can potentially go wrong if enemies happen to be inside, as when they are defeated, Tainted Lazarus will switch form. This can lead to an undesired item on one form, or a forced use of Flip.
** If an Angel Room has an item you would prefer on one form over the other, and Flip is not currently charged, using a bomb on the Angel Statue and fighting the Angel that spawns will make Tainted Lazarus flip upon the fight's completion. This does not flip the item, however.
** {{R|Challenge Room}}s and {{R|Boss Rush}} will flip Tainted Lazarus every wave.
* Active items will recharge even when the other form is active. For example, it will take 3 rooms to charge an active item that requires 3 bars to charge, despite the fact that the flipped form doesn't have the same active item. This effectively allows him to double the active item slots.
* Tainted Lazarus's strength lies in his control over his health bars. Using Flip strategically can avoid death if one form is low, save a deal chance if one character only has Red Hearts.
* If one form of Tainted Lazarus has flight and a room is cleared while above usually inaccessible land, Tainted Lazarus will gain a temporary flight for the current room.
* Greed and Greedier Modes have the following interactions with Tainted Lazarus:
** Each completed wave swaps from one form of Tainted Lazarus to the other, which locks him in the flip animation for about a second. He cannot fire tears while in this animation.
** Temporary buffs, such as {{I|The Book of Belial}} or {{P|XI - Strength}}, will disappear when switching from one character to the other.
** Clearing the room before {{e|Ultra Greed}} does not switch characters.
* Some items and trinkets with the [[Item Tags lazarussharedglobal|<code>lazarussharedglobal</code> item tag]] are shared between both forms. This includes items that map parts of the floor such as {{I|The Compass}}, items that increase devil/angel deal chance such as {{I|Black Candle}}, and items/trinkets that spawn new or altered rooms on each floor such as {{I|Voodoo Head}}. Items that grant a shared effect and a stat boost (such as {{I|Pentagram}}, which grants a damage increase and increases devil deal chance), will not transfer the stat increases between forms.
* Items that affect [[Room Clear Awards|room clear awards]] (for example, {{i|Contract From Below}}) work only when the character holding the item appears after clearing the room.
* {{I|Steam Sale}} is not shared between the two.
* During {{E|Dogma}} + {{E|The Beast}} fight, flips happen between each boss, including the Ultra Harbingers.
* While playing [[Repentance Co-Op|co-op]], Tainted Lazarus will still swap between forms while dead; if one of Tainted Lazarus' forms dies while the other is alive, he will alternate between being a ghost baby and a normal character.
** To be able to revive the dead version of Tainted Lazarus, the player must enter the boss fight while being on the alive form of the character, as the flip takes place BEFORE the revive process.
* Clearing a room under the effects of [[Paralysis]] will keep Tainted Lazarus's current state instead of switching to his counterpart.

== Item Interactions ==
* {{i|Birthright}}: Whichever version of Tainted Lazarus is not active will be available as a "ghost", moving alongside the current Tainted Lazarus like Esau, able to fire tears but immune to taking damage. Both characters receive the Birthright effect when one character collects it.
** Some effects from the inactive form's items will apply to the active form now as well. For example, {{I|Damocles}} can fall and kill the player.
*** Revival items collected by one form will work if the other dies, and will affect health of both forms upon revival (similar to {{c|Jacob and Esau}} interaction).
** If a one-room effect is triggered before a flip, the effect will be retained by the ghost for the remainder of the room. For example, if one form uses {{i|The Nail}} and then finishes the room, it will become the ghost but will still be able to crush obstacles.
** Active items gain twice as many charges from clearing rooms, though the inactive form will no longer gain charge from clearing rooms.
** The active character can be damaged by the other form's bombs such as those from {{i|Dr. Fetus}}.
** If one form has {{i|Lachryphagy}}, the other form's tears will also be absorbed but the tear will not grow.
** {{r|Boss Challenge Room}}s will require both forms to have 1 HP to enter, instead of only the active one.
** Only the form that is currently active can cross {{I|The Ladder}} when bridging a gap.
** Allows the ghostly form of Tainted Lazarus to press the wave stop button in Greed/Greedier Mode without taking damage.
* {{i|Buddy in a Box}}: The familiar changes appearance and tear effects each time the character who has Buddy in a Box is flipped to.
* {{i|Crown Of Light}}: In Greed Mode, once damage is taken, and Flip is used twice, the Crown of Light will appear visually to be active, but its effects are still disabled.
* {{i|D4}}/{{i|D8}}/{{i|D100}}: Rerolls only apply to the form holding the die.
* {{i|Deep Pockets}}: Works while either form is active.
* {{i|Genesis}}: Resets both forms' items and spawns items based on the total amount of items from both characters. Flip can be used infinitely while inside the room.
* {{t|Filigree Feather}}: Defeated angel bosses drop angel room items only for the form carrying Filigree Feather.
* {{I|Glitched Crown}}: Only works while the form holding it is active when an item spawns.
* {{I|Isaac's Tomb}}: Will only spawn the chest if the form holding it initially enters the floor.
* {{I|Kidney Stone}}: After switching in form with Kidney Stone, the effect of item will activate immediately.
* {{i|Lost Soul}}: If the Lost Soul dies, it will not respawn by switching characters. If it didn't die, going to the next floor with the character that doesn't have Lost Soul will still grant its rewards once the character is active again.
* {{I|Luna}}: The beams of light are available for either form to attain.
* {{I|Sacred Orb}}: Will only work if the version of Tainted Lazarus holding it sees the item first.
* {{i|The Stairway}}: Will work while either form is active while going down a floor.
* {{i|Star of Bethlehem}}: The star only moves while the character holding it is active, effectively making it take twice as long to reach the boss room. Additionally, if that character is inactive when entering the floor, the star will not spawn until that character becomes active, in which case it spawns in the center of the current room.
* {{I|There's Options}}: Will still grant two boss items, regardless of who fought the boss.
* {{I|TMTRAINER}}: Only generates glitched items if the form holding it is the one to see the item first. This can allow the player to get normal, unglitched items onto the form holding TMTRAINER, and glitched items onto the form without it if desired.
* {{i|Urn of Souls}}: Souls cannot be collected by an inactive character. This means that as soon as the room is cleared, all souls still in the air are lost even after you Flip.
* {{I|Vanishing Twin}}: The item is shared between both forms.
* {{I|Eternal D6}}: If the rerolled item disappears, the pedestal remains, allowing the player to still swap to acquire the ghostly item. This also applies to items from shops and devil deals, spawning the pedestal for free and allowing you to effectively "steal" the ghostly item 

=== Good Items ===
* {{I|The Battery}}: Any extra charges Flip acquires will not be lost when switching to the form without The Battery, allowing you to build up an extra activation, although at a slower than normal pace.
* {{i|Binge Eater}}: In a {{r|Devil Room}}, Tainted Lazarus is effectively able to give items to his inactive form for free by picking up a food item. This will remove one heart container, and then instantly restore it. The mirrored Devil items will remain, however, meaning he can use {{i|Flip}} and pick them up as his alternate form for no cost.
* {{i|Book of the Dead}}: Bone orbitals and charmed {{E|Bony|text=Bonies}} spawned by Book of The Dead carry over through transforming and benefit either form of Tainted Lazarus.
* Items like {{I|The Body}}, {{I|Cancer}}, and other drastic health increases allow Tainted Lazarus to tank large amounts of damage in longer boss fights if spread between forms.
* Large damage increases such as {{I|Cricket's Head}} or {{I|Synthoil}} are useful to get onto Tainted Lazarus's living form early to make up for his damage deficit.
* {{i|Chaos}} only works when the active form has it. This allows the Lazarus to control which rooms have items chosen from random item pools, by choosing which form to enter a room with.
* {{I|Diplopia}} and {{I|Crooked Penny}} allow for potential duplications of strong items to get on both forms. Though keep in mind that Devil Rooms or Angel Rooms would likely require the form holding them to be active upon entry. Locate the boss room, and if necessary, clear rooms until Flip is charged and you are playing as the form ''not'' holding Diplopia or Crooked Penny. Upon defeating the boss, Tainted Lazarus will Flip automatically, allowing the duplication of Devil or Angel Items, followed by flipping and taking the same item on the other form.
* Having one form hold {{I|Guppy's Paw}} with a medium to large pool of heart containers can extend the potential time before needing to flip, extending your health bars even further.
* {{I|Esau Jr.}}'s body granted by the item has a stronger damage, additional health, and flight.
** Esau-Lazarus's form is permanent, even if the item is left behind, allowing for a straight-up character upgrade. The only way to change back is with the item itself.
** Be careful if the item is acquired late game. The item randomization may throw off the rhythm established by that point, especially if it includes more risky items like {{I|Ipecac}} without any means of mitigation, making it nearly impossible to play with. It's highly recommended to acquire as close to the start of a new run as possible instead. Since it only has one charge though, switching back to Lazarus shouldn't be difficult in most situations.
* {{I|Jumper Cables}} can allow for more use of one form's Active Item, or just more use of Flip.
* {{I|Red Stew}}'s damage bonus does not decrease when the form holding it is inactive.
* {{I|Star of Bethlehem}} can be a good way to prevent one form from lagging behind the other power-wise.
* Offensive Active Items that charge on a timer, especially {{I|Sharp Straw}} and {{I|Glass Cannon}}, can make up tremendously for one form that happens to be lagging behind. The Sharp Straw in particular, due to how it calculates damage, can make the weaker form much more offensively viable during end game boss fights.
* {{T|Old Capacitor}}: Effectively turn Flip into a {{dlc|nr+}} 12 / {{dlc|r+}} 8-charge item (due to only being active half of the time); however, the increased spawning of Lil Batteries can allow more micromanagement to take place when a floor is finished, flipping between forms as needed.
** {{T|Watch Battery}} is a good alternative, or even supplementary trinket to keep on the other form, as it increases chances of finding Lil Batteries as well.
* Low charge Active Items with simple, effective uses, such as {{I|Shoop da Whoop!}}, {{I|White Pony}}, or {{I|Spider Butt}} can be recharged within one large room, and can supplement the lack of power Tainted Lazarus is prone to.
* {{i|Quints|nr+}} is a great choice in Greed mode, because the 5-familiar limit will reset every time Lazarus flips, while the familiars themselves stay. This allows Lazarus to amass a very large amount of familiars. {{I|Birthright}} ruins this synergy, though.
* {{I|Red Key}}: The {{r|Ultra Secret Room}} grants more items for both forms, and the red rooms provide more charges for Flip.

=== Bad Items ===
* While not exactly a bad choice, extra lives like {{I|Dead Cat}} or {{I|1up!}} require a bit more thought to get use out of, due to only reviving the form holding it. If a 1up! is found, try to have the form with more heart containers pick it up to get the most use from it.
* {{i|Blood Puppy}}: If it rages, the rage state is retained, which can cause damage from it spawning directly on the player when switching forms if the player doesn't get away in time.
* In Greed and Greedier Mode, {{i|Sprinkler}} will disappear when a new wave spawns.
* {{dlc|nr+}} {{I|Death's List}}: Bonus reward cannot be granted unless Tainted Lazarus has {{I|Birthright}}, or both his forms have a copy of Death's List.
** {{dlc|r+}} Death's List is always active as long as one form holds the item.
* {{I|4.5 Volt}}: While the two versions of Tainted Lazarus normally charge both their active items at the same time, 4.5 Volt will only charge them when the form that holds it deals damage, and will also prevent them from being charged when the other clears a room.

